<article class="env-lemma" id="04NT">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04NT">Lemma <span data-tag="04NT">67.34.4</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$. Let $n \geq 0$. Assume $f$ is locally of finite type. The set </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  W_ n = \{ x \in |X| \text{ such that the relative dimension of }f\text{ at } x \leq n\}   \]
</div>
  <p> is open in $|X|$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Choose a diagram 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ U \ar[r]_ h \ar[d]_ a &  V \ar[d] \\  X \ar[r] &  Y }  \]
</div>
    <p>
       where $U$ and $V$ are schemes and the vertical arrows are surjective and étale, see Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/02X1" data-tag="02X1">65.11.6</a>. By Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/02FZ" data-tag="02FZ">29.29.4</a> the set $U_ n$ of points where $h$ has relative dimension $\leq n$ is open in $U$. By our definition of relative dimension for morphisms of algebraic spaces at points we see that $U_ n = a^{-1}(W_ n)$. The lemma follows by definition of the topology on $|X|$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>